WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.368
Cassava is planted from stem cuttings, not seeds. Good cuttings are the cheapest way to a good harvest.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.869
Take stems from healthy plants that are about eight to twelve months old.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:17.842
Do not use stems from plants with yellow, twisted or spotted leaves. These are signs of disease.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.353
Ask your extension worker about improved local varieties.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.360
Cut pieces about twenty to twenty-five centimetres long, with five to seven buds.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.722
Use a sharp cutlass, so the ends are clean, not crushed.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.687
Keep cuttings in the shade, and plant them within a few days.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:45.878
Before you move on, check: Select stems from healthy plants. Cut 20 to 25 cm pieces. Plant within a few days.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.037
In the next lesson: Preparing the land.
